  "id": "COMPOUND:15637 - PROTEIN:5777",
  "verbalization": "Oleiferin C appears to have a shared target relationship with Thioredoxin, mitochondrial, which is subsequently targeted by multiple compounds, including Pseudopterosin Q and Tenuifolin E. These intermediates all lead to SF-188, suggesting a potential pathway where Oleiferin C may influence SF-188 through a common intermediate. The evidence indicates that Oleiferin C may act as a modulator of Thioredoxin, mitochondrial, which in turn affects SF-188 via multiple downstream targets. The integration of these pathways suggests that Oleiferin C could be involved in a broader regulatory network that impacts SF-188, possibly through a mechanism involving oxidative stress or mitochondrial function. The presence of multiple targets for Thioredoxin, mitochondrial supports the idea of a conserved or shared biological role, though the exact mechanism linking Oleiferin C to SF-188 remains to be fully elucidated.",
